    <text x="315" y="40" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="750" font-size="15" fill="#4a3abf">ExperimentConfig</text>
    <rect x="28" y="54" width="278" height="72" rx="10" fill="#fff" stroke="#cfc7f3"/>
    <text x="40" y="74" font-weight="700" font-size="12.5" fill="#4a3abf">GeometryConfig</text>
    <text x="40" y="93" font-size="11.5">zscore=True · metric=euclidean</text>
    <text x="40" y="110" font-size="10.5" fill="#777">Wasserstein ground cost · W methods only</text>
    <rect x="316" y="54" width="290" height="72" rx="10" fill="#fff" stroke="#cfc7f3"/>
    <text x="328" y="74" font-weight="700" font-size="12.5" fill="#4a3abf">SupportConfig</text>
    <text x="328" y="93" font-size="11.5">snap=True · mesh=6 · range=(-1,1)</text>
    <text x="328" y="110" font-size="10.5" fill="#777">discretisation of X</text>
    <rect x="28" y="134" width="278" height="72" rx="10" fill="#fff" stroke="#cfc7f3"/>
    <text x="40" y="154" font-weight="700" font-size="12.5" fill="#4a3abf">methods : [MethodSpec]</text>
    <text x="40" y="173" font-size="11">IPW-O-W · IPW-O-X · Hajek-O-W · Hajek-O-X</text>
    <text x="40" y="189" font-size="11">· Kallus · IPW · Policy-Opt · DR</text>
    <rect x="316" y="134" width="290" height="72" rx="10" fill="#fff" stroke="#cfc7f3"/>
    <text x="328" y="154" font-weight="700" font-size="12.5" fill="#4a3abf">run knobs</text>
    <text x="328" y="173" font-size="11">n_arms · cap · γ_true · gammas</text>
    <text x="328" y="189" font-size="11">seeds · maximize · n_train/n_test</text>
    <line x1="622" y1="119" x2="668" y2="119" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#carr)"/>
    <rect x="672" y="80" width="150" height="78" rx="12" fill="#fff" stroke="#cfcfe6"/>
    <text x="747" y="106" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" font-size="12.5">run_experiment</text>
    <text x="747" y="125" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5">method × variant</text>
    <text x="747" y="140" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5">× Γ × seed</text>
    <line x1="824" y1="119" x2="848" y2="119" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="2.5" marker-end="url(#carr)"/>
    <rect x="852" y="80" width="138" height="78" rx="12" fill="#eefaf0" stroke="#b6e3c1"/>
    <text x="921" y="104" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="700" font-size="12.5" fill="#177a41">results/&lt;exp&gt;/</text>
    <text x="921" y="124" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5">policy · outcomes</text>
    <text x="921" y="139" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10.5">+ config.json</text>
  </svg>
  </div>

  <h3>GeometryConfig — Wasserstein ground cost</h3>
  <p class="muted">Used only by the Wasserstein methods (IPW-O-W, Hajek-O-W).</p>
  <table>
  <tr><th>field</th><th>default</th><th>meaning</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code class="tip" data-tip="True — z-score covariates (scale-fair) · False — raw distances (bit-identical to the original solver)">zscore</code></td><td><code>True</code></td><td>z-score the covariates before the distance \(D\) (scale-fair). <code>False</code> ⇒ raw distances (bit-identical to the original solver).</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code class="tip" data-tip="&quot;euclidean&quot;  (the only metric implemented)">metric</code></td><td><code>"euclidean"</code></td><td>ground-cost metric for \(D\) (only euclidean is implemented).</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h3>SupportConfig — discretisation</h3>
  <table>
  <tr><th>field</th><th>default</th><th>meaning</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code class="tip" data-tip="True — snap continuous X to a grid · False — raw-X singletons (or already-discrete X, e.g. exp_c)">snap</code></td><td><code>True</code></td><td>discretise: snap \(X\) onto a grid (the solver's <code>discretize</code> switch) so the free-π LP is well-posed; <code>False</code> ⇒ raw-\(X\) singletons.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code class="tip" data-tip="4 · 6 · 8 · 10  — grid levels per coordinate (finer ⇒ more cells)">mesh</code></td><td><code>6</code></td><td>grid levels per coordinate (e.g. 6 ⇒ a 6×6 grid in 2-D).</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code class="tip" data-tip="(-1, 1) · (0, 1) · (-2, 2)  — the (lo, hi) the grid spans">mesh_range</code></td><td><code>(-1, 1)</code></td><td>(lo, hi) the grid spans, per coordinate.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code class="tip" data-tip="4 · 6 · 8  — precision for treating two X values as one cell">rounding_digits</code></td><td><code>6</code></td><td>precision at which two support points count as one cell.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h3>MethodSpec — what to compare</h3>
  <table>
  <tr><th>field</th><th>default</th><th>meaning</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code class="tip" data-tip="&quot;IPW-O-W&quot; · &quot;IPW-O-X&quot; · &quot;Hajek-O-W&quot; · &quot;Hajek-O-X&quot; · &quot;IPW-X-X&quot; · &quot;Direct-X-X&quot; · &quot;DoublyRobust-X-X&quot; · &quot;Kallus&quot;">name</code></td><td>—</td><td>one of IPW-O-W, IPW-O-X, Hajek-O-W, Hajek-O-X, IPW-X-X, Direct-X-X, DoublyRobust-X-X, Kallus.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code class="tip" data-tip="(&quot;Capped&quot;,&quot;Uncapped&quot;) · (&quot;Capped&quot;,) · (&quot;Uncapped&quot;,)  — Kallus is always (&quot;Flat&quot;,)">variants</code></td><td><code>("Capped","Uncapped")</code></td><td>which capacity variants to run. <strong>Kallus is forced to <code>("Flat",)</code></strong> — parametric, no capacity.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h3>ExperimentConfig — the run</h3>
  <table>
  <tr><th>field</th><th>default</th><th>meaning</th></tr>
  <tr><td><code class="tip" data-tip="&quot;exp_c-parity&quot; · &quot;conti2d-gamma5&quot;  — names the folder results/NAME/">experiment</code></td><td>—</td><td>name ⇒ <code>results/&lt;name&gt;/</code>.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code class="tip" data-tip="2 · 3 · 4  — must equal the DGP's number of treatments K">n_arms</code></td><td>—</td><td>number of arms \(K\) (must equal the DGP's K; <code>cap</code> length must match).</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code class="tip" data-tip="K=2: (1.0, 0.4) · K=4: (1.0, 0.4, 0.4, 0.4)  — per-arm budget; arm 0 usually 1.0; Σ cap ≥ 1">cap</code></td><td>—</td><td>per-arm capacity (length \(K\)) for the Capped variants.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code class="tip" data-tip="0 · 1 · 2 · 3 · 5  — DGP confounding strength; matched Γ = e^(γ/2)">gamma_true</code></td><td>—</td><td>DGP confounding strength; the matched \(\Gamma=e^{\gamma_{\text{true}}/2}\) is always added to the sweep.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code class="tip" data-tip="(1, 2, 3, 5, 7) · (1.0, 3.0, 7.0)  — the Γ sweep">gammas</code></td><td>—</td><td>the \(\Gamma\) sweep.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code class="tip" data-tip="(0,) · (0, 1, 2) · tuple(range(10))  — replication seeds">seeds</code></td><td>—</td><td>replication seeds.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code class="tip" data-tip="[&quot;IPW-O-W&quot;, &quot;IPW&quot;] · [MethodSpec(&quot;IPW-O-W&quot;, (&quot;Capped&quot;,)), &quot;Kallus&quot;]">methods</code></td><td>—</td><td>list of names / <code>MethodSpec</code> / dicts.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code class="tip" data-tip="GeometryConfig(zscore=True, metric=&quot;euclidean&quot;)">geometry</code> / <code class="tip" data-tip="SupportConfig(snap=True, mesh=6, mesh_range=(-1, 1))">support</code></td><td>defaults above</td><td>the GeometryConfig / SupportConfig.</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code class="tip" data-tip="True — Y is a reward · False — Y is a loss (the paper's convention)">maximize</code></td><td><code>True</code></td><td>\(Y\) is a reward (default) vs the paper's loss convention (affects Hajek-O-X/OW/Kallus only).</td></tr>
  <tr><td><code class="tip" data-tip="100 · 200 · 300 · 500">n_train</code> / <code class="tip" data-tip="400 · 600 · 800 · 2000">n_test</code></td><td><code>300 / 800</code></td><td>train / test sample sizes.</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h3>Rules &amp; conventions</h3>
  <ul>
  <li><strong>Matched Γ</strong> \(=e^{\gamma_{\text{true}}/2}\) is always sampled in the sweep (the operating point).</li>
  <li><strong>Validation:</strong> <code>cap</code> length must equal <code>n_arms</code>; method names ∈ the known set; metric ∈ {euclidean}.</li>
  <li><strong>Capability gating:</strong> <code>geometry</code> (zscore/metric) reaches only IPW-O-W &amp; Hajek-O-W; <code>maximize</code> reaches only Hajek-O-X, Hajek-O-W, Kallus; other methods ignore knobs they don't accept.</li>
  <li><strong><code>obj_kind</code>:</strong> each saved objective is tagged (worst-case value / regret / robust-AIPW / clairvoyant) — <em>not</em> cross-comparable.</li>
  <li><strong>Clean guard:</strong> re-running an experiment name prunes stale method/variant/Γ outputs left by a prior, different config.</li>
  <li><strong>No true propensities:</strong> weights are always estimated from \((X,T)\) — never \(e_{\text{true}}\)/\(S\).</li>
  <li>The <strong>GUI</strong> (<code>application/</code>, Streamlit) lets you set all of this on its Config page; <code>n_arms</code> is sourced from the DGP page so the two can't disagree.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Example</h3>
  <pre><code>from common.config import ExperimentConfig, GeometryConfig, SupportConfig, MethodSpec

cfg = ExperimentConfig(
    experiment="exp_c-parity", n_arms=4, cap=(1.0, 0.4, 0.4, 0.4),
    gamma_true=3.0, gammas=(1.0, 3.0, 5.0, 7.0), seeds=(0, 1, 2),
    methods=["IPW-O-W", "IPW-O-X", "IPW-X-X", MethodSpec("DoublyRobust-X-X", variants=("Capped",))],
    geometry=GeometryConfig(zscore=True),            # Wasserstein ground cost
    support=SupportConfig(snap=True, mesh=6),         # discretisation
    maximize=True, n_train=300, n_test=800,
)
run_experiment(cfg, generate)                        # writes results/exp_c-parity/ + config.json
</code></pre>
</div>

