      </div>
      <h4 style="margin:14px 0 4px;font-size:1.02rem">Deployed policy \(\pi(\text{treat}\mid X)\) (Γ + seed dropdowns)</h4>
      <div class="ichart" id="ichart-ow3-cap_policy" style="max-width:900px"></div>
    </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mbox mbox-note"><div class="mbox-l">Finding</div>
    <p>This is the cleanest OW-dominance result: at \(\Gamma\approx1.5\) (uncapped) / \(\Gamma\approx2\) (capped),
    <strong>both IPW-O-W and DoublyRobust-O-W exceed the best of all other methods</strong> (DoublyRobust-O-X tops the
    field at \(\approx0.56\text{-}0.58\); both OW reach \(\approx0.60\text{-}0.62\)), in both regimes, at a small
    \(\Gamma\) well below the matched \(\Gamma\approx5\). On \(\varepsilon\): the tight radius is best here; enlarging
    it makes DoublyRobust-O-W over-conservative. The mechanism is the synergy design: large common \(S\)-effect
    cripples the outcome-model methods, the small differential keeps the effect subtle, and the \(S\)-\(X\) correlation
    lets covariate balancing win.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="muted" style="margin-top:14px">Artifacts: <code>assets/exp_owwin3/{dgp.py, run_owwin3.py, build_owwin3.py}</code> · chart data <code>owwin3_charts.json</code> · results <code>owwin3_results.json</code> · search/verify <code>assets/exp_dgp_search/search_owbest.py, verify_I.py</code> · PNGs. Discrete X (7 levels), \(S\in\{-1,+1\}\), logistic propensity, \(N_{\text{train}}=700\); both regimes.</p>
  </div>

